{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"ADR DRAFTED — docs/adr/0055-jira-family-sub-seam.md, plus the 0035 amendments, architecture.md,\nuser-guide.md; env-vars.md regenerates with ZERO diff. make lint 0, make typecheck 0.\n\nTHE DRAFT FOUND A FOURTH STALE SITE I HAD MISSED. I identified three places where ADR 0035 asserts the\nfirst real second backend is out of scope (:111 diagram comment, :204-205 prose, :236-237 Decision\nitem 6). There is a FOURTH in Consequences — 'Standing up the first such backend is scoped to epic\nbe74' — carrying the same falsified claim. Also annotated section (c)'s 'everything under it is one\nbackend's implementation', which jira_family/ now makes untrue. So the AC's 'all three' was itself an\nundercount; the correct answer is four sites plus one annotation.\n\nONE AC NOT SATISFIED, and the reason corrects a diagnosis I stated publicly: 'the documented commands\nhave been executed against the J5 harness' could not be done on this workstation. The harness README\n(lines 54-73) documents that the base image is linux/amd64 ONLY, that docker-compose pins\nplatform: linux/amd64, and that 'a native amd64 runner is a HARD REQUIREMENT for a run that\ncompletes, not a preference' — with THREE prior measured attempts on this project's own arm64\nworkstation. This machine is Apple Silicon.\nMy two local harness timeouts earlier in this session were therefore ARCHITECTURE EMULATION, not the\nresource contention I attributed them to and wrote into the loop's standing notes. The answer was\ndocumented in the repo the whole time and I diagnosed without reading it. That AC needs the\nnative-x86_64 jira-dc-harness CI job, which is where the README says the evidence belongs.\n\nAlso fixed while verifying the draft: _backend.py's docstring said the core reached for 'eighteen'.\nRe-measured — the core reaches for TWENTY-ONE; eighteen is the always-required subset the Protocol\ndeclares; the other four are the opt-in capability surface. Both numbers were right, the sentence\nconflated them. Same drift that produced this ticket's own AC mismatch two rounds ago."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785509530067343001,"uuid":"ac4c734c-5203-42e8-bcc0-094ab465a51e"}